      --------------------------- UList ---------------------------
OK about a week ago I saw someone had written a userlist program...  And I
thought  it would be cool to have a userlist program that had configurable
output  based  on the same idea as my bdays program.  So here it is.  This
is  just a preliminary release and only has some of the variables in it...
It  can't  print  any  date  variables  at  all...   I'm  about to move to
California,  but  in  about mid-May you can look for updates...  Maybe not
until  late  May...   Anyway,  here's  a  list  of the variables currently
supported:

%a      Address
%A      Access Level
%b      Balance
%c      CityState
%C      Country
%h      Handle
%m      Comment
%n      Newline
%N      Account Number
%p      Phone Number
%P      Password
%r      Real Name
%s      Serial Number
%S      Sex
%z      Zip-Code
%%      Actually print %

Numbers  can be placed in-between the % and the character specifier in the
same format as printf() uses...

%20h would print:
"Spaceman            "
%-20h would print:
"            Spaceman"

It  should all be fairly self-explanatory...  This is a DOS program...  It
supports multiple configurations.  Name the files "sysdata:ulist00.config"
and  just  replace the 00 with the number config you want that to be.  All
config numbers must be consecutive.  The configuration file format is:

Line 1: Title
     2: Header
     3: User 1/4
     4: User 2/4
     5: User 3/4
     6: User 4/4
     7: Footer

--- Let me know if you have any comments, suggestions, or bug-reports!
